.nh
.TH hclapi 8

.SH NAME
.PP
hclapi - Type-safe, declarative API runtime powered by HCL.


.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
hclapi

.PP
\fBUsage\fP:

.PP
.RS

.nf
hclapi [GLOBAL OPTIONS] [command [COMMAND OPTIONS]] [ARGUMENTS...]

.fi
.RE


.SH COMMANDS
.SH serve, s
.PP
Start the HTTP API server from compiled manifests

.PP
\fB--config, -c, --manifests, -m\fP="": Manifest file, directory, or glob pattern (can be specified multiple times)

.PP
\fB--host, -H\fP="": Host address to bind the listener (overrides manifest)

.PP
\fB--log-format\fP="": Log output format (text, json) (default: "text")

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="": Log level (debug, info, warn, error) (default: "info")

.PP
\fB--port, -p\fP="": Port to bind the listener (overrides manifest) (default: 0)

.PP
\fB--verbose, -v\fP: Enable debug logging (shorthand for --log-level=debug)

.SH openapi, oas, spec
.PP
Export OpenAPI 3.1 specification for the compiled manifests

.PP
\fB--config, -c\fP="": Manifest file, directory, or glob pattern

.PP
\fB--format, -f\fP="": Output format (json, yaml) (default: "json")

.PP
\fB--output, -o\fP="": Write output to a file instead of stdout

.SH lint, check, validate
.PP
Validate manifest schemas, types, and referential integrity

.PP
\fB--config, -c\fP="": Manifest file, directory, or glob pattern

.SH routes
.PP
List all compiled endpoints and pipeline step sequences

.PP
\fB--config, -c\fP="": Manifest file, directory, or glob pattern

.SH version, v
.PP
Print version and build metadata

.PP
\fB--short, -s\fP: Print only the semantic version string
